Article 4 (Persons Eligible to Use VIP Lounges)
(1) The following persons may use VIP lounges: <Amended on March 23, 2013; October 16, 2015; September 26, 2016>
1. The President and former Presidents;
2. The Speaker of the National Assembly, Chief Justice of the Supreme Court, President of the Constitutional Court, Prime Minister, Chairperson of the National Election Commission, former Speakers of the National Assembly, former Chief Justices of the Supreme Court, former Presidents of the Constitutional Court, former Prime Ministers, and former Chairpersons of the National Election Commission;
3. Representatives of political parties having negotiating groups in the National Assembly;
4. Any of the following persons recommended by the Minister of Foreign Affairs upon determination that special courtesies are necessary:
  (a) Heads of diplomatic missions in the Republic of Korea;
  (b) Representatives of international organizations;
  (c) Foreign nationals corresponding to persons under subparagraphs 1 through 3;
  (d) Foreign ministers or other foreign nationals of ministerial rank or higher;
5. Persons performing schedules related to official duties whom the President of Incheon International Airport Corporation under Article 2 of the Incheon International Airport Corporation Act or the President of Korea Airports Corporation under Article 2 of the Korea Airports Corporation Act recognizes as appropriate.
(2) Spouses and children of persons eligible to use VIP lounges under paragraph (1) may use the VIP lounge together with the distinguished guest.
